{
  "$comment": [
    "NEUTRAL EXAMPLE agent organisation matching the shipped product configuration.",
    "",
    "config/agent-org.json is the checked-in neutral product default. It contains no",
    "installation-specific fleet or owner directives, is classified open, and is included",
    "in a customer's private Cloud Mirror with the runnable engine.",
    "",
    "This example is a schema-shaped reference for tooling and documentation. Runtime and",
    "tests read config/agent-org.json directly; a missing shipped configuration is an",
    "error to repair, not a reason to substitute an installation-specific file.",
    "",
    "A seat here is a DECLARATION, not a claim that credentials exist for it. The",
    "fleet view renders declared agents and the surrounding copy already forces the",
    "declared-versus-observed distinction, so declaring a seat you have no provider",
    "login for is consistent with what the graph promises it means.",
    "",
    "The controller id stays neutral. agent.spawn binds its authenticated transport",
    "actor to a fresh dispatch-only projection; setup does not persist one client",
    "family as the controller. Claude worker seats therefore start at claude-1.",
    "",
    "Customers may edit their installation's declared seats without changing who owns",
    "or supplies the dedicated private repository configured for Cloud Mirror."
  ],
